# Grid row actions (unified)

In `school-management-unified` data tables and grids, **row actions stay in a 3-dot menu**. Do not put Edit / Delete / Archive as standalone text links in the actions column.

## Trigger

- Use `RowActionsMenu` (`src/components/RowActionsMenu.vue`).
- Icon-only 3-dot `fk-iconbtn` with translated `aria-label` (e.g. `$t('common.actions')`).
- Dots must be **filled circles** (`fill="currentColor"`). Do not use the faint Heroicons stroke path (`M12 5v.01…`) — it disappears on light rows.
- Default placement is **up** (`bottom-full`) so the menu is not clipped by the next card. Use `placement="down"` only when the row is at the top of a scroll area with room below.

## Menu items

- Each item is `RowActionsItem` with an **icon and a label**.
- Built-in icons: `edit`, `delete`, `activate`, `archive`, `restore`.
- Destructive actions use `danger` (red text).
- Labels are translated (`$t('common.edit')`, `$t('common.delete')`, etc.).
- **Claim-gate mutations:** hide Edit / Delete / assign actions with `v-if="hasClaim('page_key', 'edit')"` (or the matching action). Do not show an action the user’s group cannot perform.

## Card overflow

Do not put `overflow-hidden` on the card or table wrapper that contains the menu, or the popup will be clipped. Prefer `overflow-visible` on `fk-table-wrap`.
